   "id": "inclusive-tier-ceilings-enter-next-policyengine-bracket-at-equality",
   "concept": "us:policies/income_tax/savers_credit_pipeline#federal_savers_credit",
   "kind": "amount_difference",
   "disposition": "upstream_engine_gap",
   "mechanism": "PE-US 1.767.3 stores Notice 2025-67's correct 2026 joint ceilings ($48,500/$52,500/$80,500) and the correct filing-status adjustments. They are encoded as lower bounds of the next brackets, and PolicyEngine Core 3.30.3 digitizes the scale exclusively at equality. Section 25B(b) and the Notice instead make every published ceiling inclusive. Thus the five exact 50% ceilings return 20%, the three exact 20% ceilings return 10%, and the three exact 10% ceilings return zero in PolicyEngine.",
